# <%= @app_module %>

An agent built on the [Lemon](https://github.com/z80dev/lemon) platform.

## Run the tests

    mix deps.get
    mix test

No API key required. The suite scripts the model at the `stream_fn` seam
(`test/support/fake_llm.ex`), so the loop, the tools and the tool registry are
all exercised for real while the network is not.

## Talk to a real model

    export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
    mix run --no-halt -e "<%= @app_module %>.Console.start()"

The provider and model come from `config/config.exs`, or from
`<%= String.upcase(@app) %>_PROVIDER` and `<%= String.upcase(@app) %>_MODEL` at
runtime. Any provider `LemonAi.Models` knows about will do; each reads its own key
from the environment.

## Layout

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `lib/<%= @app %>/agent.ex` | The model, system prompt and tool list. Start here. |
| `lib/<%= @app %>/tools/word_count.ex` | One tool, and the contract the rest follow. |
| `lib/<%= @app %>/console.ex` | A terminal channel; a worked example of the event stream. |
<%= if @channel? do %>| `lib/<%= @app %>/channel.ex` | A `LemonChannels.Plugin`, the platform's channel extension point. |
<% end %><%= if @memory? do %>| `lib/<%= @app %>/memory.ex` | Durable memory across runs, on `lemon_memory`. |
<% end %>| `test/support/fake_llm.ex` | The scripted model that makes the suite runnable offline. |

